{
 "title": "Fire",
 "summary": "A stylized flame: a subdivided sphere pulled up into a flame with soft selection, a Displace modifier (Voronoi texture on an empty's coordinates, the empty driven up by #frame/10) so the shape churns; an emission shader coloured by a gradient (Y-rotated mapping) through a white-to-red colour ramp, masked by a voronoi that rises with another empty (#frame/8) plus a flipped gradient so only the top is eaten into tongues (greater than -> mix shader with transparent; the voronoi stretched upward so the holes read as tongues). Embers: a larger copy with its own material, a faster empty (#frame/6+5), the gradient multiplied so only thin tips at the top show.",
 "objects": [
  {
   "name": "Fire",
   "description": "the flame"
  },
  {
   "name": "Embers",
   "description": "the ember shell"
  }
 ],
 "expected_result": "An animated cartoon flame on a dark background: white-yellow core, orange-red tongues flickering upward, sparks of ember at the top.",
